WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:03:08.530
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
03:08.800 --> 03:11.520
But if you ever hurt Papang like this again,

3
03:12.120 --> 03:13.000
I won't let it go.

4
03:13.080 --> 03:15.320
When I hate someone,

5
03:15.400 --> 03:17.080
I hate them until the day I die.

6
03:17.880 --> 03:21.920
I told you. I'm Ramil's wife.

7
03:22.000 --> 03:24.040
PREVIOUSLY

8
03:24.120 --> 03:25.880
How about I take you to your parents?

9
03:26.640 --> 03:27.920
I'll help you out.

10
03:37.040 --> 03:37.960
Papang.

11
03:38.560 --> 03:40.760
Daddy's going to work now. Bye.

12
03:41.400 --> 03:42.680
-Be a good boy. -Bye.

13
03:43.400 --> 03:44.920
-Let's go. -Alright.

14
03:46.600 --> 03:47.880
Papang.

15
03:48.400 --> 03:50.680
Mommy brought your game.

16
03:50.760 --> 03:51.600
Come on.

17
03:52.200 --> 03:54.000
-What are you doing? -Well…

18
03:54.080 --> 03:55.440
Did you change your mind?

19
03:56.040 --> 03:57.120
I'm going with you.

20
03:57.200 --> 03:58.520
What are you going to do?

21
03:59.440 --> 04:01.960
Want to go home instead? I can drop you off.

22
04:02.720 --> 04:04.920
I'm going with you.

23
04:05.000 --> 04:06.280
I'm going to work.

24
04:06.880 --> 04:09.400
My son and I won't interfere with your work.

25
04:09.480 --> 04:11.560
The development is huge.

26
04:11.640 --> 04:14.000
I also want to pay my respects to Mr. Pichai.

27
04:14.080 --> 04:17.040
Papang, do you miss Great-Grandpa Pichai?

28
04:17.120 --> 04:19.600
Yes. He's very kind.

29
04:20.920 --> 04:23.240
Let's go. I don't want to make you late for work.

30
04:25.160 --> 04:26.080
Hathaya.

31
04:26.600 --> 04:30.520
Carry that basket and bring those things over there too.

32
04:34.240 --> 04:37.840
Can't do it? If you can't, Papang and I can carry them ourselves.

33
04:37.920 --> 04:40.400
It's okay. I'll carry them.

34
04:44.840 --> 04:46.560
Let's go, Daddy.

35
04:47.200 --> 04:48.040
Come on.

36
04:48.840 --> 04:50.400
Let's get in the car.

37
04:56.320 --> 04:57.440
Hey,

38
04:58.120 --> 05:00.960
take Papang to my office first. I need to check on the workers.

39
05:04.560 --> 05:06.840
Everyone, come over here, please.

40
05:10.440 --> 05:12.040
Hathaya, bring the basket here.

41
05:19.240 --> 05:20.800
I made sandwiches for everyone.

42
05:22.400 --> 05:24.480
Boss, your friend is really nice.

43
05:24.560 --> 05:26.960
I'm not his friend.

44
05:27.480 --> 05:30.160
My name is Nuchwara. I'm Papang's mother

45
05:30.680 --> 05:33.400
and your boss's wife.

46
05:35.120 --> 05:37.520
Everyone, get back to work.

47
05:37.600 --> 05:38.480
Go.

48
05:45.080 --> 05:45.960
Papang.

49
05:47.040 --> 05:48.480
-Daddy has to work now. -Okay.

50
05:48.560 --> 05:49.520
Be good, all right?

51
05:50.440 --> 05:51.480
Give Daddy a kiss.

52
06:03.960 --> 06:05.920
I'm going to get to work too.

53
06:07.040 --> 06:08.360
Carry the basket and follow me.

54
06:08.440 --> 06:10.880
And get the things from the trunk too.

55
06:18.400 --> 06:19.520
Hello, Grandpa.

56
06:19.600 --> 06:21.240
-Hello, Great-Grandpa. -Hello.

57
06:21.320 --> 06:22.480
Hello.

58
06:23.400 --> 06:25.600
-Hello, Great-Grandpa. -Hello, my dear.

59
06:25.680 --> 06:26.760
Hello.

60
06:27.800 --> 06:31.040
I haven't seen you in a long time. You've grown so much.

61
06:31.120 --> 06:33.320
Are you doing well?

62
06:33.400 --> 06:35.120
I want you to stay strong.

63
06:35.200 --> 06:36.720
Why is that?

64
06:37.240 --> 06:40.800
So you can carry me around the whole development.

65
06:40.880 --> 06:42.800
I'm too old for that now.

66
06:42.880 --> 06:45.760
But I have a golf cart. Want me to drive you around in that?

67
06:46.360 --> 06:49.080
-Yes. Let's go. -Okay.

68
06:50.520 --> 06:52.080
Hathaya, give me the basket.

69
07:00.600 --> 07:01.640
Let's go.

70
07:02.560 --> 07:04.080
Grandpa,

71
07:04.160 --> 07:08.440
I brought you sandwiches, chicken salad, and fresh orange juice.

72
07:08.520 --> 07:10.040
Thank you.

73
07:10.120 --> 07:11.880
I just felt like having that.

74
07:11.960 --> 07:14.960
Can I take a picture with you? I've missed you.

75
07:20.720 --> 07:21.880
-Take our picture. -Come on.

76
07:33.400 --> 07:34.360
Let's take a picture.

77
07:36.800 --> 07:39.200
One, two, three.

78
07:41.800 --> 07:43.000
Good.

79
07:43.520 --> 07:46.520
-How have you been, Grandpa? -I've been well.

80
07:46.600 --> 07:47.880
Then…

81
07:48.600 --> 07:50.040
I'll get back to work.

82
07:51.840 --> 07:53.760
Come on. Let's go for a ride.

83
07:53.840 --> 07:55.320
Let's go.

84
07:55.840 --> 07:57.920
Let's go have some fun.

85
08:03.160 --> 08:05.480
I really have to thank you both

86
08:05.560 --> 08:06.800
for being so generous.

87
08:06.880 --> 08:09.560
Look at my crew.

88
08:09.640 --> 08:11.640
They're working day and night

89
08:11.720 --> 08:13.280
without getting tired.

90
08:13.360 --> 08:15.520
That's the power of overtime pay.

91
08:15.600 --> 08:17.800
At this rate, the work will be finished quickly.

92
08:18.760 --> 08:21.000
Don't let what happened yesterday happen again.

93
08:21.080 --> 08:23.240
If the houses aren't finished by the contract date,

94
08:23.320 --> 08:25.320
I'll have to pay a fortune in penalties.

95
08:26.520 --> 08:27.920
Don't worry, madam.

96
08:28.000 --> 08:29.840
You can trust me.

97
08:29.920 --> 08:31.880
I won't disappoint you or Miss Chayanee.

98
08:33.679 --> 08:35.400
Money really is wonderful.

99
08:35.480 --> 08:36.520
It can buy almost anything.

100
08:36.600 --> 08:38.240
But believe it or not, miss,

101
08:38.919 --> 08:39.919
money can't buy me.

102
08:40.960 --> 08:42.159
For me,

103
08:43.840 --> 08:46.160
it's all heart. Give me yours, and I'll give you mine.

104
08:49.520 --> 08:52.600
You and Madam treat me this well,

105
08:52.680 --> 08:53.960
and I'll work my hardest for you.

106
08:57.000 --> 08:59.800
Come on. Faster.

107
09:00.320 --> 09:03.200
-Keep working hard. -Madam. Madam.

108
09:03.280 --> 09:04.240
Miss Chayanee.

109
09:04.320 --> 09:06.600
What is it, Chamoi? What's wrong with you?

110
09:08.240 --> 09:09.800
What is it now?

111
09:10.400 --> 09:12.960
I just wanted Madam and Miss Chayanee

112
09:13.040 --> 09:14.680
to have a good laugh too.

113
09:17.240 --> 09:18.360
Have you lost your mind?

114
09:18.440 --> 09:20.640
What are you laughing at?

115
09:20.720 --> 09:22.120
Hathaya

116
09:22.200 --> 09:24.840
has officially been pushed aside.

117
09:28.240 --> 09:31.200
Madam, Ramil's real wife is here.

118
09:31.280 --> 09:33.120
She's been going around telling everyone

119
09:33.200 --> 09:35.600
she's Ramil's wife.

120
09:37.480 --> 09:39.600
I completely forgot

121
09:39.680 --> 09:42.240
Ramil already had a wife.

122
09:42.320 --> 09:45.640
Well, this is going to expose that whole fake marriage, isn't it?

123
09:46.400 --> 09:47.960
Wait. Where are you going?

124
09:49.000 --> 09:50.240
I'm going to work.

125
09:51.440 --> 09:54.240
You don't look fit to work at all.

126
09:55.560 --> 09:58.320
Maybe you should see a veterinarian.

127
10:00.760 --> 10:02.000
Madam?

128
10:02.520 --> 10:05.120
Why would she need a veterinarian?

129
10:06.240 --> 10:08.360
Because she's a sick dog nobody wants anymore.

130
10:08.440 --> 10:10.360
She needs treatment.

131
10:12.320 --> 10:13.160
Mom.

132
10:14.480 --> 10:15.680
A veterinarian

133
10:15.760 --> 10:18.360
can't treat that.

134
10:18.440 --> 10:19.640
You'd have to cremate it.

135
10:24.440 --> 10:25.760
Where are you rushing off to?

136
10:26.960 --> 10:28.160
The temple.

137
10:29.840 --> 10:31.400
Going to have yourself cremated?

138
10:34.800 --> 10:36.640
I'm going to make merit.

139
10:36.720 --> 10:40.120
I thought I'd dedicate some merit to wicked spirits.

140
10:42.160 --> 10:43.480
Madam,

141
10:43.560 --> 10:45.920
she was trying to insult you.

142
10:47.120 --> 10:50.800
I know. She's the one who's going to die of a broken heart

143
10:50.880 --> 10:52.880
and become a wicked spirit.

144
10:52.960 --> 10:54.040
Exactly.

145
10:56.240 --> 10:59.120
Papang, be good for Great-Grandpa.

146
10:59.200 --> 11:00.080
P.C. PROPERTY

147
11:01.000 --> 11:04.160
It's been a long time. How have you been?

148
11:06.000 --> 11:10.160
If I weren't doing well, I probably wouldn't be standing here.

149
11:13.000 --> 11:15.760
Is that how friends greet each other?

150
11:16.960 --> 11:18.680
Did you ever consider me a friend?

151
11:20.920 --> 11:25.000
I forgot. We were just people who happened to be in the same class.

152
11:25.520 --> 11:26.520
Not friends.

153
11:27.040 --> 11:28.840
Are you still angry with me

154
11:29.920 --> 11:33.640
because I liked Raiwin, the same man you liked?

155
11:34.720 --> 11:36.480
Why would I be angry?

156
11:37.000 --> 11:40.000
Raiwin wasn't interested in you, so you went back to Ramil.

157
11:40.080 --> 11:41.400
You really are something.

158
11:41.480 --> 11:43.880
You only go after rich men's sons.

159
11:43.960 --> 11:47.240
Then you got yourself pregnant and had to drop out of college.

160
11:47.320 --> 11:49.120
But the pathetic part is that in the end,

161
11:49.200 --> 11:52.480
all you got was a useless stepson who'll never amount to anything.

162
12:00.800 --> 12:02.120
What are you laughing at?

163
12:03.120 --> 12:05.040
If you knew the truth,

164
12:05.760 --> 12:07.800
you'd probably cry your eyes out.

165
12:09.280 --> 12:10.520
What are you talking about?

166
12:13.040 --> 12:14.960
Chayanee is so smart.

167
12:15.040 --> 12:16.400
Good at everything.

168
12:17.000 --> 12:19.680
If you want to know, investigate it yourself.

169
12:20.400 --> 12:22.200
If I told you,

170
12:22.280 --> 12:24.240
you might go into shock.

171
12:25.480 --> 12:27.160
Take care of yourself.

172
12:28.240 --> 12:29.520
Because

173
12:30.560 --> 12:32.440
I've moved into Ramil's house now.

174
12:33.200 --> 12:34.800
Let's see who survives this.

175
12:41.040 --> 12:42.520
You're Chayanee's mother, right?

176
12:43.960 --> 12:45.160
Yes.

177
12:45.760 --> 12:47.920
I hope you don't mind if I don't greet you properly.

178
12:48.560 --> 12:51.040
I'm not Chayanee's friend.

179
12:52.320 --> 12:56.320
But I do have one thing to tell you. When you have time,

180
12:56.400 --> 13:00.400
take your daughter to wash her mouth out. It's incredibly filthy.

181
13:01.280 --> 13:02.560
That was harsh.

182
13:03.840 --> 13:04.840
Really harsh.

183
13:04.920 --> 13:08.520
Who is that foul-mouthed woman?

184
13:19.160 --> 13:21.120
She was someone I knew in college.

185
13:22.640 --> 13:24.360
She used to chase Raiwin,

186
13:24.440 --> 13:26.160
but he wasn't interested in her.

187
13:26.680 --> 13:29.160
Then she got pregnant and dropped out.

188
13:30.440 --> 13:32.200
Ramil claimed the baby as his,

189
13:32.720 --> 13:35.960
but they lived separately. Ramil would only visit the child once in a while.

190
13:38.120 --> 13:39.400
Now I remember.

191
13:39.480 --> 13:42.240
She brought that child here to play with Father before.

192
13:42.320 --> 13:44.640
She has a vicious mouth.

193
13:44.720 --> 13:47.880
Miss Chayanee, you need to get rid of her and send her far away.

194
13:51.840 --> 13:53.920
If you knew the truth,

195
13:54.640 --> 13:56.680
you'd probably cry your eyes out.

196
13:57.600 --> 14:00.360
If you want to know, investigate it yourself.

197
14:01.080 --> 14:05.040
If I told you, you might go into shock.

198
14:05.680 --> 14:07.440
The way she threatened me just now…

199
14:07.520 --> 14:10.720
It sounded like there's some secret I don't know.

200
14:10.800 --> 14:13.400
Don't pay any attention to her.

201
14:13.480 --> 14:16.360
Actually, I think it's good that she came back to Ramil.

202
14:17.600 --> 14:19.240
How is that good, madam?

203
14:24.640 --> 14:27.120
She can get rid of Hathaya for us.

204
14:27.200 --> 14:29.240
Then we won't have to waste our own energy.

205
14:29.320 --> 14:31.720
Let those two women tear each other apart.

206
14:36.320 --> 14:39.600
Hathaya will get pressured from every direction

207
14:40.360 --> 14:44.240
until she can't take it anymore and runs back to the countryside on her own.

208
14:53.560 --> 14:55.360
Sir, I'm sorry

209
14:55.440 --> 14:59.040
that Nuchwara and Papang came to work like this.

210
15:00.880 --> 15:03.520
I thought you and Nuchwara

211
15:03.600 --> 15:05.640
were separated and had no obligations.

212
15:06.240 --> 15:08.200
That's why I allowed Hathaya to stay with you.

213
15:09.280 --> 15:11.080
So how did this happen?

214
15:12.800 --> 15:14.840
I didn't expect Nuchwara

215
15:15.480 --> 15:17.320
to bring Papang and move in either.

216
15:18.400 --> 15:19.960
You know why

217
15:20.040 --> 15:22.160
I agreed to claim Papang as my son.

218
15:23.120 --> 15:25.160
I know how much you sacrificed.

219
15:25.760 --> 15:27.760
But now you're not alone anymore.

220
15:28.400 --> 15:30.600
Hathaya is living with you too.

221
15:33.760 --> 15:35.480
No matter how much you insist,

222
15:36.000 --> 15:38.280
there's nothing between the two of you,

223
15:39.280 --> 15:43.120
everyone else believes you're husband and wife.

224
15:43.720 --> 15:47.120
I want you to take responsibility for Hathaya's feelings too.

225
15:48.720 --> 15:49.760
Yes, sir.

226
15:50.400 --> 15:51.240
Papang.

227
15:52.240 --> 15:53.200
Come on.

228
15:53.880 --> 15:57.360
I will take you to see the pond in the development.

229
15:57.440 --> 15:59.480
-Want to go? -Yes.

230
15:59.560 --> 16:01.560
Come on. Take this with you too.

231
16:03.000 --> 16:04.000
Let's go.

232
16:27.240 --> 16:28.400
Hathaya.

233
16:30.560 --> 16:31.800
How are you doing?

234
16:32.560 --> 16:34.480
I'm okay.

235
16:35.080 --> 16:38.960
Has Nuchwara bothered you again?

236
16:39.840 --> 16:43.640
If she said or did anything inappropriate, I'm sorry.

237
16:45.360 --> 16:48.160
I already told you. No matter what happens, I'm on your side.

238
16:54.160 --> 16:55.760
It's lunchtime. Come eat with me.

239
16:58.560 --> 16:59.400
Let's go.

240
17:00.320 --> 17:01.480
Ramil.

241
17:03.480 --> 17:05.640
I brought lunch for you.

242
17:11.720 --> 17:13.920
Thanks. But you go ahead and eat first.

243
17:14.760 --> 17:16.960
Come eat with us. Your son is waiting.

244
17:23.440 --> 17:26.160
Hathaya, come eat with us.

245
17:26.240 --> 17:27.720
I brought enough for you too.

246
17:30.760 --> 17:31.760
Come on.

247
17:33.080 --> 17:33.920
Come on.

248
17:50.160 --> 17:54.000
-Come on, Hathaya. Eat with us. -I made your favorite too.

249
18:03.360 --> 18:04.560
Hathaya.

250
18:04.640 --> 18:07.040
Could you feed Papang for me?

251
18:10.080 --> 18:14.000
Papang, let Aunt Hathaya feed you.

252
18:20.320 --> 18:21.400
You eat first.

253
18:21.480 --> 18:22.800
No. I'll feed you.

254
18:22.880 --> 18:24.360
-Come on. It's good. -I'll do it.

255
18:25.560 --> 18:26.680
I want to feed you.

256
18:37.320 --> 18:38.240
Is it good?

257
18:47.960 --> 18:49.240
Hathaya.

258
18:49.320 --> 18:51.000
Wash the food containers

259
18:51.080 --> 18:52.840
and the other things for me.

260
18:53.960 --> 18:54.800
Okay.

261
18:56.640 --> 18:58.640
And give Papang a bath too.

262
18:58.720 --> 19:00.120
He's all sweaty and sticky.

263
19:00.200 --> 19:02.120
Why don't you bathe your own son?

264
19:03.320 --> 19:05.760
I just got back from work. I'm tired.

265
19:08.960 --> 19:10.360
I'll bathe him.

266
19:11.920 --> 19:13.280
Go.

267
19:15.880 --> 19:19.400
Come on, Papang. Come with me.

268
19:20.280 --> 19:22.280
You've been working so hard.

269
19:22.360 --> 19:24.680
Come sit over here.

270
19:24.760 --> 19:26.080
Come on.

271
19:29.520 --> 19:31.280
I'll give you a massage.

272
19:33.720 --> 19:36.400
Your shoulders look tense.

273
19:36.480 --> 19:39.040
You must be stressed.

274
19:41.040 --> 19:42.120
What should I do about that?

275
19:48.440 --> 19:50.680
Papang, we're out of soap.

276
19:50.760 --> 19:52.240
I'll run downstairs and get some.

277
19:56.280 --> 19:59.440
You hardly look any different from when we were in college.

278
20:00.040 --> 20:02.240
But I like you better now.

279
20:03.880 --> 20:05.240
You're more attractive.

280
20:07.640 --> 20:08.760
What are you doing?

281
20:09.720 --> 20:10.840
I'm going

282
20:11.600 --> 20:14.240
to take off your shirt so you can cool down.

283
20:15.160 --> 20:16.960
Then I'll massage you.

284
20:17.480 --> 20:18.440
No.

285
20:18.960 --> 20:21.520
Come on. Don't upset your wife.

286
20:22.120 --> 20:23.400
That's enough.

287
20:24.360 --> 20:25.360
Let go.

288
20:27.760 --> 20:31.680
I regret ever being obsessed with your brother.

289
20:32.440 --> 20:34.040
If I could go back,

290
20:34.640 --> 20:36.080
I would choose you instead.

291
20:37.680 --> 20:40.080
I think I would've been much happier.

292
20:41.040 --> 20:42.520
But it doesn't matter now.

293
20:44.480 --> 20:48.080
Because the two of us are a family anyway.

294
20:48.680 --> 20:50.440
You're my husband.

295
20:51.760 --> 20:54.680
Stop fantasizing. You know none of this is real.

296
20:56.680 --> 20:58.200
Then I'll make it real.

297
20:58.720 --> 20:59.720
Get off me.

298
21:01.520 --> 21:03.360
Why do you have to treat me like this?

299
21:04.200 --> 21:05.920
I have to lie to everyone

300
21:06.640 --> 21:08.040
and say you're my wife.

301
21:11.360 --> 21:14.280
But I can't lie to myself. I have never loved you.

302
21:14.360 --> 21:15.680
And I never will.

303
21:17.240 --> 21:19.040
Then can't you open your heart to me?

304
21:20.280 --> 21:23.000
I want us to be a real family

305
21:24.200 --> 21:25.200
for our son.

306
21:25.800 --> 21:29.360
Stop using Papang as an excuse. What you're doing

307
21:30.320 --> 21:32.680
is offering yourself up to get what you want.

308
21:33.640 --> 21:35.960
Stop clinging to rich men like you always have.

309
21:45.400 --> 21:47.120
Then what am I supposed to do?

310
21:48.160 --> 21:51.840
How am I ever supposed to have a comfortable life like everyone else?

311
21:53.320 --> 21:54.840
First,

312
21:55.560 --> 21:58.120
stop comparing your life to everyone else's.

313
21:59.080 --> 22:00.840
If you want a comfortable life,

314
22:01.840 --> 22:05.560
you have to build it yourself. Stop looking for a shortcut.

315
22:08.480 --> 22:09.920
And all this time,

316
22:10.960 --> 22:13.000
I've constantly helped you solve your problems.

317
22:13.520 --> 22:14.880
You should have learned from it

318
22:15.400 --> 22:16.880
and changed yourself.

319
22:18.200 --> 22:19.120
Listen to me.

320
22:20.880 --> 22:23.360
You can't depend on me for the rest of your life.

321
22:24.120 --> 22:27.480
One day, I'm going to have my own life. My own family.

322
23:26.400 --> 23:27.800
Where are Nuchwara and Papang?

323
23:28.800 --> 23:31.400
I haven't seen Nuchwara come out of her room yet.

324
23:31.480 --> 23:32.960
She must be really upset.

325
23:38.000 --> 23:39.320
I had to say those things.

326
23:40.800 --> 23:42.440
I've helped her enough.

327
23:43.240 --> 23:45.280
She has to start solving her own problems.

328
23:50.560 --> 23:52.040
If this had been before,

329
23:52.960 --> 23:54.960
I probably would've thought you were cruel.

330
23:56.000 --> 23:58.280
But now that I know the whole story,

331
23:59.520 --> 24:00.760
I understand.

332
24:08.320 --> 24:09.600
I love Papang.

333
24:12.040 --> 24:14.320
And I care deeply about his feelings.

334
24:17.960 --> 24:20.120
When the time is right,

335
24:20.880 --> 24:23.280
I think we should tell Papang the truth.

336
24:24.520 --> 24:27.120
He has a right to know his own story.

337
24:33.520 --> 24:34.360
Papang.

338
24:35.720 --> 24:36.760
Come on. Let's eat.

339
24:37.560 --> 24:38.960
I'm taking Papang away.

340
24:40.040 --> 24:42.600
-Where? -Back to my house.

341
24:45.040 --> 24:47.720
Hey, Hathaya.

342
24:50.080 --> 24:52.120
If you're willing to help,

343
24:52.200 --> 24:55.160
carry the bags and take Papang to the car.

344
24:55.760 --> 24:56.920
-Okay. -I'll do it.

345
25:02.360 --> 25:05.440
Papang, come eat first. Come with me.

346
25:08.040 --> 25:09.040
Are you hungry?

347
25:18.440 --> 25:20.120
You're heartless.

348
25:20.200 --> 25:22.320
You're not even going to ask me to stay?

349
25:23.840 --> 25:25.160
Just because I don't stop you

350
25:25.240 --> 25:27.400
doesn't mean I don't care about Papang.

351
25:27.920 --> 25:29.880
I just think this is the best solution.

352
25:30.480 --> 25:31.760
Just because I'm leaving

353
25:32.640 --> 25:34.600
doesn't mean I agree with you.

354
25:37.680 --> 25:40.800
People aren't born with the same advantages.

355
25:40.880 --> 25:42.840
You expect me to start over now?

356
25:42.920 --> 25:44.280
It's too late.

357
25:46.440 --> 25:48.680
Hard work is for diligent people.

358
25:49.200 --> 25:52.320
Shortcuts are for smart people.

359
25:56.400 --> 25:57.360
Whatever you say.

360
26:01.680 --> 26:02.800
Oh.

361
26:09.040 --> 26:12.360
I don't want to go. I'm going to miss you, Daddy.

362
26:13.920 --> 26:16.880
Come on. Daddy will miss you too.

363
26:16.960 --> 26:18.040
How about this?

364
26:18.120 --> 26:19.800
Daddy will video call you every day.

365
26:19.880 --> 26:21.880
Promise?

366
26:22.480 --> 26:23.280
I promise.

367
26:25.000 --> 26:26.160
Good boy.

368
26:31.400 --> 26:34.160
Take care. We'll see each other soon.

369
26:34.240 --> 26:36.600
Are you going to miss me too?

370
26:36.680 --> 26:38.200
Of course.

371
26:38.280 --> 26:40.880
I'll be so lonely without you around.

372
26:41.560 --> 26:42.640
No one left to argue with.

373
26:45.520 --> 26:47.840
When I come back, I'll argue with you again.

374
27:02.720 --> 27:05.920
Just because I'm leaving doesn't mean I'm giving up.

375
27:08.200 --> 27:09.880
I'll be back.

376
27:39.840 --> 27:40.800
Hey.

377
27:45.000 --> 27:46.840
Is something wrong?

378
27:46.920 --> 27:48.640
You've barely spoken since we left home.

379
27:49.640 --> 27:50.760
No.

380
27:51.880 --> 27:54.160
If something is wrong, you can tell me.

381
27:56.920 --> 27:57.760
I'm going to work.

382
28:11.280 --> 28:12.680
Where did all the workers go?

383
28:13.640 --> 28:16.240
Pong, where are your workers?

384
28:16.320 --> 28:17.600
Why aren't they here?

385
28:17.680 --> 28:19.560
I've been calling them,

386
28:20.080 --> 28:22.800
but the other contractor sent pickups to pick them up.

387
28:22.880 --> 28:24.480
What is that supposed to mean?

388
28:24.560 --> 28:27.920
It means the other site is paying more,

389
28:28.000 --> 28:29.640
so they all went over there.

390
28:29.720 --> 28:31.760
I'm already paying them plenty.

391
28:31.840 --> 28:33.800
What else do they want? I'm not paying more.

392
28:34.520 --> 28:36.680
Pong, you're responsible for this.

393
28:37.280 --> 28:38.680
Madam,

394
28:38.760 --> 28:40.960
I already called them.

395
28:41.040 --> 28:42.920
I called other contractors too,

396
28:43.000 --> 28:44.920
but nobody is available.

397
28:46.360 --> 28:48.200
How about

398
28:49.960 --> 28:51.800
we try another approach?

399
28:52.400 --> 28:53.240
What approach?

400
28:54.280 --> 28:56.480
Could you add

401
28:57.360 --> 28:59.000
another 50 baht?

402
28:59.080 --> 29:01.120
I'll tell them. I'm sure they'll come back--

403
29:01.200 --> 29:02.560
I'm not paying any more.

404
29:04.040 --> 29:04.920
Mom.

405
29:06.840 --> 29:08.640
Pong has caused damage to the project.

406
29:08.720 --> 29:11.160
Fire him and find another crew.

407
29:13.520 --> 29:16.280
Calm down. It isn't fair to blame Pong.

408
29:16.360 --> 29:18.720
Those workers are the ones who abandoned the job.

409
29:19.480 --> 29:21.360
But Pong is the foreman.

410
29:22.160 --> 29:23.720
He has to take responsibility.

411
29:25.520 --> 29:26.360
Pong,

412
29:26.440 --> 29:29.440
go get those workers back here.

413
29:29.520 --> 29:31.240
Before Father finds out.

414
29:32.560 --> 29:33.600
Yes, madam.

415
29:33.680 --> 29:35.480
Come on. Let's go back to the office

416
29:35.560 --> 29:36.840
before he inspects the site.

417
29:36.920 --> 29:38.120
Madam.

418
29:38.200 --> 29:40.160
What? I'm in a hurry.

419
29:40.240 --> 29:41.280
Well…

420
29:41.360 --> 29:42.560
Move.

421
29:46.080 --> 29:47.280
Where did all the workers go?

422
29:50.960 --> 29:53.880
Father, I'm sorry.

423
29:53.960 --> 29:56.320
There was a small accident.

424
29:56.880 --> 30:00.040
The workers' vehicle broke down, so they couldn't come in today.

425
30:00.120 --> 30:01.280
Their vehicle broke down?

426
30:02.160 --> 30:04.600
-Yes. -Or did they abandon this job?

427
30:07.240 --> 30:10.720
I noticed no one was working here,

428
30:10.800 --> 30:13.000
so I asked some workers I know.

429
30:13.080 --> 30:16.800
They said the foreman here

430
30:16.880 --> 30:20.440
told the crew to stop working and go work on another project.

431
30:20.520 --> 30:23.760
I want to know who gave that order.

432
30:29.120 --> 30:30.600
It wasn't me, sir.

433
30:31.120 --> 30:33.880
You know how much effort I put into this place.

434
30:35.280 --> 30:37.120
The contractor they're talking about

435
30:37.200 --> 30:39.400
must be an old contractor.

436
30:39.480 --> 30:41.040
He's notorious for abandoning jobs.

437
30:41.120 --> 30:44.320
If you knew the old contractor was unreliable,

438
30:44.400 --> 30:46.600
why did you bring him onto my project?

439
30:50.360 --> 30:51.440
Father,

440
30:51.520 --> 30:54.280
you can't really blame Pong.

441
30:54.880 --> 30:58.120
Another development was probably jealous of ours

442
30:58.200 --> 31:01.520
and deliberately offered our workers more money to steal them away.

443
31:03.160 --> 31:05.200
Stop blaming other people.

444
31:05.280 --> 31:09.120
You were the one who brought Pong to me

445
31:09.640 --> 31:12.000
and guaranteed that he was such a professional.

446
31:12.520 --> 31:14.520
A real professional doesn't operate like this.

447
31:19.080 --> 31:21.520
-Ramil. -Yes, sir.

448
31:22.360 --> 31:25.000
From now, you're responsible for overseeing all the work here.

449
31:26.160 --> 31:27.040
Of course, sir.

450
31:27.120 --> 31:29.440
Father, what about Pong?

451
31:30.040 --> 31:31.360
Pong will work under Ramil.

452
31:34.080 --> 31:36.600
Ramil has full authority over this entire project.

453
31:43.640 --> 31:44.760
Grandpa,

454
31:45.400 --> 31:46.760
could you come to the office?

455
31:46.840 --> 31:48.080
What now?

456
31:51.080 --> 31:53.400
Chayanee's customers were denied financing.

457
31:53.480 --> 31:55.360
They're asking for their deposits back.

458
32:04.600 --> 32:05.640
Hello.

459
32:05.720 --> 32:07.840
I'm Pichai, the owner of this development.

460
32:07.920 --> 32:09.240
How can I help you?

461
32:09.320 --> 32:11.040
Your granddaughter

462
32:11.120 --> 32:12.720
said anyone applying

463
32:12.800 --> 32:14.920
for financing here would be approved.

464
32:15.000 --> 32:17.920
I paid the reservation deposit, but the bank rejected my application.

465
32:19.480 --> 32:20.600
I'm sorry.

466
32:20.680 --> 32:24.160
There must have been some mistake. I can contact another bank for you.

467
32:24.240 --> 32:25.280
No.

468
32:25.360 --> 32:27.120
I want my deposit back.

469
32:27.200 --> 32:29.600
You promised full refunds if financing was denied.

470
32:30.200 --> 32:33.120
Pay me now, or I'll complain to Consumer Protection

471
32:33.200 --> 32:34.280
and take this all the way.

472
32:34.360 --> 32:37.320
Of course. I'll refund every customer in full.

473
32:38.280 --> 32:39.120
Hathaya,

474
32:39.200 --> 32:41.720
take them to process their refunds.

475
32:42.320 --> 32:43.360
Yes, Grandpa.

476
32:43.440 --> 32:45.680
I apologize for the mistake.

477
32:46.280 --> 32:47.880
Don't make promises you can't keep.

478
32:50.440 --> 32:51.560
This way, please.

479
32:52.720 --> 32:53.600
This way.

480
32:54.960 --> 32:55.840
Please have a seat.

481
32:59.800 --> 33:00.840
Grandpa,

482
33:01.440 --> 33:03.080
I can contact other banks.

483
33:03.160 --> 33:05.880
I'll find one that's willing to approve their loans.

484
33:07.760 --> 33:10.480
Bring me the customers' reservation forms.

485
33:10.560 --> 33:11.600
Yes, sir.

486
33:19.720 --> 33:25.400
HOME FOR SALE FROM 4.8 MILLION BAHT

487
33:27.120 --> 33:28.040
What did they say?

488
33:28.120 --> 33:30.680
None of the financing applicants were approved.

489
33:30.760 --> 33:32.240
We must refund all their deposits.

490
33:34.960 --> 33:36.160
Mr. Pichai must be furious.

491
33:46.200 --> 33:49.080
You raised the wages for Pong's crew.

492
33:50.160 --> 33:51.800
How can Ramil manage his workers now?

493
33:52.400 --> 33:54.480
Management needs one consistent standard.

494
33:56.520 --> 33:58.200
Father,

495
33:58.280 --> 34:00.280
we had to pay them more

496
34:00.360 --> 34:02.080
to get them back to work.

497
34:02.680 --> 34:03.640
And then what?

498
34:04.360 --> 34:05.880
You give them more once,

499
34:05.960 --> 34:08.600
and the next time they'll bargain for even more.

500
34:09.840 --> 34:13.000
You can call me stupid if you want,

501
34:13.080 --> 34:14.960
but everything Chayanee and I did

502
34:15.040 --> 34:17.320
was to make sure our project succeeded.

503
34:17.400 --> 34:18.719
Was that really wrong?

504
34:19.880 --> 34:22.760
If you had done it correctly, I wouldn't have said a word.

505
34:23.520 --> 34:25.880
If you don't know how to manage people, then don't do it.

506
34:31.800 --> 34:33.679
Grandpa, don't blame Mom.

507
34:34.280 --> 34:37.480
I was the one who agreed to Pong's proposal.

508
34:37.560 --> 34:38.800
It was my fault.

509
34:39.400 --> 34:40.480
And you.

510
34:41.360 --> 34:43.120
I told you repeatedly that

511
34:43.679 --> 34:47.400
with the economy declining like this, you must not use that promotion.

512
34:48.480 --> 34:51.560
But those customers were referred by Uncle Saksit.

513
34:51.639 --> 34:54.159
I didn't think there would be a problem.

514
34:55.719 --> 34:57.400
When you run a business,

515
34:57.920 --> 34:59.760
you have to examine every angle.

516
34:59.840 --> 35:02.000
You cannot operate based purely on trust.

517
35:06.280 --> 35:09.280
Every one of those customers has significant debt.

518
35:12.520 --> 35:15.880
Their incomes are unstable.

519
35:16.560 --> 35:18.600
Their existing debt levels are already high.

520
35:19.480 --> 35:21.920
More than 40 reservations have now been canceled.

521
35:22.000 --> 35:25.000
We have to start all over again and find new customers.

522
35:25.080 --> 35:26.560
See how much damage this has caused?

523
35:27.880 --> 35:29.880
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

524
35:29.960 --> 35:33.520
I promise this will never happen again.

525
35:35.080 --> 35:37.360
Instead of apologizing, you should study

526
35:37.440 --> 35:39.920
how other people think and learn from their good ideas.

527
35:41.640 --> 35:43.320
These are Hathaya's reservations.

528
35:45.720 --> 35:48.080
Her customers were approved and paid in full.

529
35:53.040 --> 35:56.360
From now on, Hathaya will be fully in charge of sales.

530
36:07.240 --> 36:08.640
I won't accept this, Mom.

531
36:09.920 --> 36:12.720
Hathaya already handles the marketing plan,

532
36:12.800 --> 36:16.760
helps check the accounts, and now Father is giving her sales too.

533
36:16.840 --> 36:18.960
Ramil controls all the workers.

534
36:20.160 --> 36:22.240
Everything is in their hands.

535
36:23.320 --> 36:24.440
I won't accept it.

536
36:26.960 --> 36:27.920
Sweetheart.

537
36:28.760 --> 36:31.120
Grandpa. Grandpa.

538
36:31.200 --> 36:35.040
You can't suddenly give someone what belonged to Mom and me.

539
36:38.200 --> 36:41.440
The someone is also my granddaughter.

540
36:42.080 --> 36:43.880
But you said yourself

541
36:43.960 --> 36:45.640
that you didn't trust Hathaya.

542
36:45.720 --> 36:48.480
You said she inherited bad blood from her mother.

543
36:49.800 --> 36:50.800
Yes.

544
36:51.400 --> 36:53.880
I said that because I misunderstood her.

545
36:54.960 --> 36:58.080
But Hathaya has proved herself now.

546
36:58.160 --> 36:59.920
She isn't like that.

547
37:00.720 --> 37:02.080
I understand that now.

548
37:02.600 --> 37:06.160
And I refuse to be an old man who carries prejudice until the day he dies.

549
37:06.840 --> 37:08.080
I have to make this right.

550
37:10.800 --> 37:14.040
I'm going to let Hathaya manage this project.

551
37:15.680 --> 37:16.960
Chayanee,

552
37:17.040 --> 37:20.240
calm down. Get a hold of yourself. We need to figure out what to do.

553
37:20.320 --> 37:22.800
No, Mom, I won't accept this.

554
37:23.400 --> 37:24.240
Grandpa.

555
37:24.320 --> 37:26.520
Careful. Grandpa could fall.

556
37:33.880 --> 37:35.720
Grandpa. Grandpa.

557
37:36.360 --> 37:38.720
You can't give my work to someone else.

558
37:38.800 --> 37:39.920
I won't accept it.

559
37:41.320 --> 37:42.560
I've made my decision.

560
37:42.640 --> 37:45.680
Grandpa, give me another chance.

561
37:45.760 --> 37:47.680
Give your favorite granddaughter another chance.

562
37:50.240 --> 37:52.040
It's because I love you

563
37:52.920 --> 37:56.000
that I've given in to you again and again.

564
37:57.000 --> 37:59.640
From now on, if you want me to trust you,

565
37:59.720 --> 38:01.280
start a new business

566
38:01.360 --> 38:03.320
and prove to me that you can succeed.

567
38:06.640 --> 38:09.440
No. I want to manage this project.

568
38:09.520 --> 38:12.400
I won't let anyone take what belongs to me.

569
38:12.480 --> 38:14.040
I won't accept it, Grandpa.

570
38:14.840 --> 38:16.880
Chaya!

571
38:20.920 --> 38:21.920
Sir!

572
38:26.840 --> 38:27.880
Grandpa.

573
38:33.480 --> 38:35.040
Grandpa. Are you hurt?

574
39:16.120 --> 39:18.960
You can leave Grandpa here.

575
39:19.040 --> 39:21.920
Chayanee and I will take care of him.

576
39:22.960 --> 39:24.440
Father,

577
39:24.520 --> 39:27.160
I prepared a room for you downstairs,

578
39:27.240 --> 39:29.640
so you won't have to keep going up and down the stairs.

579
39:29.720 --> 39:34.000
Chayanee, help Grandpa to his room. Come on.

580
39:34.080 --> 39:35.640
I don't need either of you.

581
39:45.520 --> 39:46.760
Grandpa,

582
39:47.760 --> 39:50.320
I know you're angry with me.

583
39:52.160 --> 39:54.640
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to do it.

584
39:56.680 --> 39:58.800
I'm truly sorry, Grandpa.

585
40:00.280 --> 40:02.600
I don't know what else I can do

586
40:02.680 --> 40:04.600
to make you forgive me.

587
40:10.800 --> 40:13.680
You have to accept Hathaya moving back into this house.

588
40:20.600 --> 40:22.800
You were the one who asked me

589
40:23.640 --> 40:25.680
to make Hathaya live somewhere else.

590
40:27.240 --> 40:29.280
I agreed because you asked me to.

591
40:30.080 --> 40:32.640
You promised you would change.

592
40:33.400 --> 40:35.840
But you couldn't keep that promise.

593
40:37.680 --> 40:40.280
As far as I'm concerned, your request is no longer valid.

594
40:47.880 --> 40:48.760
Hathaya.

595
40:52.880 --> 40:54.080
Yes, Grandpa.

596
40:55.680 --> 40:58.120
While I'm recovering,

597
40:59.200 --> 41:02.400
move back in here. Help take care of me.

598
41:07.320 --> 41:09.720
And help manage the development.

599
41:21.040 --> 41:22.720
Thank you, Grandpa.

600
41:24.680 --> 41:26.400
I'll do everything I can.

601
41:27.360 --> 41:29.600
Thank you so much.

602
41:31.800 --> 41:33.880
Ramil. Let's go.

603
42:06.800 --> 42:08.880
When I think about it, I can't help laughing.

604
42:09.600 --> 42:11.880
Sometimes my life feels like I'm constantly moving.

605
42:12.480 --> 42:14.720
Your life does sound interesting.

606
42:14.800 --> 42:15.760
Quite an adventure.

607
42:17.000 --> 42:18.920
But maybe

608
42:20.000 --> 42:22.600
this will be your last move.

609
42:24.320 --> 42:27.520
I can tell Mr. Pichai has finally opened his heart to you.

610
42:28.080 --> 42:30.080
He probably wants you to live there

611
42:30.600 --> 42:34.360
as his granddaughter.

612
42:36.720 --> 42:40.160
I want to be with Grandpa. I want to take care of him.

613
42:41.920 --> 42:44.720
That's good. But…

614
42:47.120 --> 42:48.680
you need to be very careful.

615
42:48.760 --> 42:51.120
Liu and Chayanee

616
42:51.640 --> 42:53.200
are extremely unhappy with you.

617
42:54.320 --> 42:57.520
But I've never tried to take their inheritance.

618
42:57.600 --> 42:59.320
They don't think the way you do.

619
43:01.400 --> 43:04.960
If anything happens, tell me immediately.

620
43:08.160 --> 43:09.120
Let's go.

621
43:16.160 --> 43:17.680
Give me the bag.

622
43:19.080 --> 43:20.400
I'll take you over there.

623
43:20.480 --> 43:23.240
And we're going to pick up someone important to you too.

624
43:26.440 --> 43:27.760
-Who? -Come on.

625
43:30.680 --> 43:34.600
Ann, you don't need to bother.

626
43:34.680 --> 43:36.320
Don't try to stop me.

627
43:36.400 --> 43:39.200
Mr. Pichai ordered me to prepare this room for Miss Hathaya.

628
43:40.560 --> 43:42.560
Listen to you calling her

629
43:42.640 --> 43:45.080
Miss Hathaya so proudly. Please.

630
43:45.160 --> 43:47.080
He's letting her stay here

631
43:47.160 --> 43:50.400
as a worker, not as his beloved granddaughter.

632
43:51.000 --> 43:53.880
Is that so, Housekeeper Chamoi?

633
43:54.760 --> 43:57.800
Why are you acting so smug with me?

634
43:57.880 --> 44:00.840
You should use that tiny brain of yours once in a while.

635
44:01.840 --> 44:05.280
If he didn't love and accept Miss Hathaya,

636
44:05.360 --> 44:07.880
do you really think he would let her move back here?

637
44:07.960 --> 44:10.360
Think. Come on. Think.

638
44:11.080 --> 44:14.320
Before long, your bosses

639
44:14.400 --> 44:18.360
might be the one who gets pushed aside.

640
44:18.440 --> 44:20.680
That was harsh.

641
44:20.760 --> 44:23.200
You do not get to insult my madam and Miss Chayanee.

642
44:23.800 --> 44:25.720
I warned you before.

643
44:26.440 --> 44:29.400
Everything can change.

644
44:29.480 --> 44:33.760
Madam and Miss Chayanee used to rule this house.

645
44:34.720 --> 44:36.680
But before long,

646
44:38.600 --> 44:40.920
you may be the one in trouble.

647
44:41.000 --> 44:43.760
Don't threaten me. I'm not scared.

648
44:43.840 --> 44:46.000
My madam

649
44:46.080 --> 44:47.960
will always protect me.

650
44:48.040 --> 44:49.640
The real question is

651
44:49.720 --> 44:51.680
how long Hathaya will last here.

652
44:51.760 --> 44:54.360
She'll probably get thrown out again just like last time.

653
44:54.440 --> 44:55.280
Chamoi.

654
44:55.360 --> 44:57.360
I already told you

655
44:57.440 --> 44:59.080
not to act smug

656
44:59.160 --> 45:00.360
or raise your voice at me.

657
45:00.440 --> 45:01.520
Why not?

658
45:01.600 --> 45:02.960
We'll see

659
45:03.040 --> 45:05.760
who ends up

660
45:05.840 --> 45:08.240
running this house.

661
45:11.120 --> 45:12.000
Where are you going?

662
45:12.080 --> 45:13.640
Come back and finish this argument.

663
45:13.720 --> 45:15.840
It's annoying here.

664
45:15.920 --> 45:18.320
I'm going to welcome Miss Hathaya.

665
45:19.440 --> 45:21.880
Annoying? What's annoying?

666
45:21.960 --> 45:24.480
The sound of a dog barking.

667
45:26.120 --> 45:29.240
Hey. I'm not a dog! If you've got the nerve, come back here.

668
45:35.720 --> 45:37.920
Here it is, Grandma. Grandpa's house.

669
45:39.080 --> 45:39.920
Hello,

670
45:40.000 --> 45:42.560
Grandma Duangjai. Do you remember me?

671
45:43.720 --> 45:45.960
I'll be straight with you. No.

672
45:46.040 --> 45:47.080
I'm old.

673
45:47.160 --> 45:48.680
We met

674
45:48.760 --> 45:50.960
when Hathai first came to live here.

675
45:51.040 --> 45:52.360
Then we met again

676
45:52.440 --> 45:55.000
after she gave birth to Miss Hathaya.

677
45:56.680 --> 45:57.920
Now I remember.

678
45:58.560 --> 46:00.960
You were the one who helped raise Hathaya.

679
46:02.200 --> 46:03.440
That's right.

680
46:04.560 --> 46:06.560
Aunt Ann, I'm bringing her to live here with me.

681
46:06.640 --> 46:08.000
Really?

682
46:08.080 --> 46:09.360
That's wonderful.

683
46:09.440 --> 46:11.400
I'll take very good care of her.

684
46:12.280 --> 46:13.400
Thank you.

685
46:13.480 --> 46:16.120
-Come in. -Come on. Let's go, Grandma.

686
46:18.000 --> 46:19.760
-I'll take the bags. -Thanks.

687
46:19.840 --> 46:21.440
What is this?

688
46:22.440 --> 46:25.720
Father said you could move back in.

689
46:25.800 --> 46:27.640
Now you're bringing your relative too?

690
46:28.360 --> 46:30.560
Exactly, madam.

691
46:30.640 --> 46:33.200
Give someone an inch and they take a mile.

692
46:35.080 --> 46:36.760
You're Liu, right?

693
46:36.840 --> 46:38.080
Hello.

694
46:38.600 --> 46:40.520
You're still as beautiful as ever.

695
46:42.200 --> 46:45.240
And you must be Chamoi. I remember you.

696
46:46.160 --> 46:48.600
Why? Because I'm still beautiful?

697
46:48.680 --> 46:50.400
Your mouth is still as nasty as ever.

698
46:54.480 --> 46:55.560
Mom,

699
46:56.400 --> 46:59.160
Hathaya probably isn't bringing Grandma here to live.

700
46:59.240 --> 47:02.040
She's probably just dropping her off. Hathaya,

701
47:02.120 --> 47:05.320
now that you're here, she can go home.

702
47:18.920 --> 47:20.120
Hathaya.

703
47:20.200 --> 47:21.520
Bring your grandma back out here.

704
47:21.600 --> 47:22.960
I said come back out.

705
47:23.040 --> 47:23.960
Mom.

706
47:24.040 --> 47:25.600
She's openly challenging us now.

707
47:26.120 --> 47:27.280
She's gone too far.

708
47:28.480 --> 47:29.360
Come on.

709
47:30.680 --> 47:31.600
Wait.

710
47:31.680 --> 47:34.320
Put those bags down, Ann.

711
47:34.400 --> 47:35.520
Chamoi.

712
47:35.600 --> 47:37.560
What?

713
47:37.640 --> 47:39.040
Hathaya.

714
47:39.120 --> 47:40.520
Hathaya. Didn't you hear me?

715
47:40.600 --> 47:42.600
Take your grandmother back home.

716
47:44.960 --> 47:47.520
I'm the one who told Hathaya to bring her grandmother here.

717
47:49.280 --> 47:50.760
Hello, sir.

718
47:51.360 --> 47:53.840
Thank you so much

719
47:53.920 --> 47:56.960
for paying for my hospital treatment

720
47:57.040 --> 48:00.080
and for being kind enough to let me stay here too.

721
48:00.680 --> 48:02.040
There's no need to be formal.

722
48:02.920 --> 48:04.600
You're practically family to me.

723
48:05.720 --> 48:06.760
Father,

724
48:07.280 --> 48:10.400
why did you have Hathaya bring her grandmother here too?

725
48:10.480 --> 48:12.200
Exactly, Grandpa.

726
48:12.280 --> 48:14.640
Hathaya alone is already enough of a burden.

727
48:16.920 --> 48:20.040
Hathaya helps me with a great deal of work here.

728
48:20.680 --> 48:21.680
And she does it well.

729
48:23.800 --> 48:27.960
If you think Hathaya is a burden,

730
48:28.840 --> 48:32.880
then perhaps you should think carefully about who the real burdens are.

731
48:39.360 --> 48:40.720
Hathaya,

732
48:40.800 --> 48:43.560
your grandmother has traveled a long way. She must be tired.

733
48:44.080 --> 48:45.600
Take her to rest.

734
48:47.960 --> 48:49.800
Yes, Grandpa. Excuse us.

735
48:56.120 --> 48:57.680
I'd like to go rest too.

736
48:57.760 --> 48:59.720
Go help Grandpa.

737
48:59.800 --> 49:01.240
Ramil, take me.

738
49:04.480 --> 49:05.520
Yes, sir.

739
49:12.880 --> 49:13.960
Mom.

740
49:14.640 --> 49:16.320
I hate her.

741
49:17.360 --> 49:19.000
Today she brought her grandmother here.

742
49:19.720 --> 49:22.720
Next thing you know, she'll bring her mother here to live too.

743
49:22.800 --> 49:25.800
Chayanee, don't let Grandpa hear you say that.

744
49:25.880 --> 49:27.800
We'll be in trouble.

745
49:28.400 --> 49:30.360
For now, just watch them.

746
49:30.440 --> 49:32.280
We'll deal with them later.

747
49:37.760 --> 49:41.720
Where are you rushing off to? Your husband said you give a great massage.

748
49:41.800 --> 49:43.760
But you were rude to me first.

749
49:43.840 --> 49:45.800
How could you put up with that?

750
49:46.400 --> 49:49.680
As long as I have a roof over my head, that's enough.

751
49:49.760 --> 49:52.760
And as long as I get to be with my granddaughter,

752
49:53.400 --> 49:54.520
I could even live under a bridge.

753
49:54.600 --> 49:56.560
-Grandma. -Mom.

754
49:57.120 --> 49:59.040
-Grandma. -Mom.

755
49:59.120 --> 50:01.040
NEXT EPISODE

756
51:59.400 --> 52:04.600
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
